{
 "id": "SHW-17",
 "name": "terrain",
 "version": 1,
 "title": "Little island: a 3D terrain with a sea-level slider",
 "summary": "A procedural island on a block of earth, drawn in 3D from one height formula (two Gaussian hills plus sine ripples): flat-shaded low-poly bands of beach sand, grass, forest, rock and snow, sixteen cone trees, a turquoise shallows ring with white surf and a deep-blue sea block whose level a slider sets. The camera drifts round with the clock and a drag orbits it; day sky in light, starry night in dark, a hidden-line wireframe in mono.",
 "prompt": "Make a little 3D world: a procedural island coloured by elevation (water, sand, grass, rock, snow) that slowly turns, which I can drag round, with a slider for the sea level.",
 "level": 5,
 "family": "SHW",
 "hand_built": "One height expression is repeated per colour band (a min() at each band's top) and the shallows, surf, beach and tree visibility all follow the live sea level; Scene3D and Chart3D have no surface coloured by bands that move with a slider.",
 "capabilities": {
  "primary": [
   "3d.surface",
   "3d.scene",
   "input.drag"
  ],
  "secondary": [
   "3d.mesh",
   "time.animation",
   "data.loop",
   "data.array",
   "draw.gradient",
   "a11y.labels"
  ]
 },
 "use_cases": [
  "generative-art",
  "game"
 ],
 "form_factor": "phone",
 "keywords": [
  "3d",
  "terrain",
  "landscape",
  "island",
  "height field",
  "heightmap",
  "procedural",
  "low poly",
  "elevation bands",
  "sea level",
  "water level",
  "diorama",
  "orbit",
  "slider",
  "showcase",
  "little world"
 ],
 "teaches": [
  "Elevation bands with one formula: each band is a meshExpression3D (surface general, x = u, z = v) whose y is min(h, top); drawn lowest band first, the strict depth test makes every point take the lowest band that reaches its height, so sand, grass, forest, rock and snow need no per-vertex colour",
  "Bands that follow a live value: the beach's top is @sea + 0.035, the shallows are min(h + 0.1, @sea + 0.002) and the surf min(h + 0.03, @sea + 0.003), so raising the sea moves the coast, the beaches and the surf together; trees scale to 0 below @sea + 0.045",
  "A diorama skirt: a general surface one grid ring wider than the land, x = clamp(-1, 1, u), whose outer ring drops to the base, gives vertical earth walls; the sea is a unit cube scaled to the live level and inset 0.003 so the earth wall stays in front of it",
  "Trees are one cone drawn in a loop over a float array of [x, y, z, scale] (positions sampled on the grass by the generator), 16 draws instead of 16 meshes",
  "The slider stays usable under a full-screen 3D view: the 3D canvas fills a column above a 76 dp spacer, and the slider (earlier in the document, so the 3D reads its live @sea) sits in that gap; the camera uses windowWidth() / windowHeight() because the 3D buffer is the window's",
  "Sky: a theme colour gradient, and 40 seeded stars whose colour is transparent in light and white in dark; mono replaces the scene with one hidden-line wireframe of max(h, @sea) and stops the drift"
 ],
 "pitfalls": [
  "3D support has not landed in androidx yet (coming): this plays in the C++ and TypeScript players only. Don't use it for a screen that must play on Android today",
  "A 3D canvas on top of a slider takes its touches (a drag on the slider orbits the island instead): keep the 3D canvas out of the slider's area",
  "The slider is a touchExpression with the absolute-position stop mode: on release it coasts with the finger's speed, so a quick flick overshoots to the end; tests release with vx 0",
  "meshExpression3D surfaces are rebuilt every frame in both players (no cache), so the drift costs eight 41 x 41 to 43 x 43 grids of a 75-token height expression a frame (about 14,000 evaluations), plus seven full-window composites and 16 tree draws: fine on a phone, heavy for a watch",
  "The 40 stars use seed()/rand(): the C++ and TypeScript players scatter them differently (the rest of the picture matches to within a few pixels)"
 ],
 "java_difference": "3D support has not landed in androidx yet (coming): the Java JSON parser does not know camera3D, lights3D, matrix3D, meshPrimitive3D or drawMesh3D; plays in the C++ and TypeScript players",
 "inputs": {
  "variables": {
   "sea": {
    "min": -0.2,
    "max": 0.4
   }
  }
 },
